{"availability":"available","full":"kgtceo/run-insights","name":"run-insights","description":"Grounded single-run analysis + coaching feedback — a deterministic analyzer computes split, fade and HR-decoupling, and the LLM's feedback can only cite the real numbers (a grounding filter drops any hallucinated stat). Eval harness. Illustrative demo. FastAPI + Next.js.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-27T18:46:27Z","updated":"2026-07-27T19:22:50Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://run-insights-pi.vercel.app","topics":["ai","anthropic","evals","fastapi","fitness","grounding","llm","nextjs","python","running"],"demo":"https://run-insights.kareemghazal.com/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:24.047Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:24.047Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:24.047Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T18:23:24.047Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Next.js","Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Enter a run's per-km splits (or \"Load sample\") and get the objective facts — split, pace fade, HR decoupling, effort type — plus a short coaching note grounded in exactly those numbers. (First run 10–20s.)","Illustrative demo — not coaching or medical advice. It summarises objective numbers from a single run; it doesn't know your training history, health, or goals. Synthetic data only.","Feed it one run's splits — a list of {km, pace, hr} plus total distance and elevation. A deterministic analyzer (pure arithmetic, no LLM) computes:"],"features":["split — negative if the 2nd half was faster, positive if slower;","pace fade — % slowdown of the last km vs the first;","HR drift / decoupling — the 2nd-half HR:pace ratio vs the 1st half (>5% flags aerobic decoupling);","effort type — easy / tempo / interval / long, from the pace variability vs the run's own median;"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/kgtceo/run-insights/blob/main/README.